  "schema": 3,
  "description": "Batch 7: the why gate and the credential read. Every case carries a why a competent agent might actually write, because the earlier round used one generic reason and that made the pass cases fail for the wrong reason. Three findings: a fluent reason unlocked rm -rf ~ and git clean -xfd until the why layer was closed for removals with no recovery path; reading a credential file is worth a question whether or not the head is exempt; and script hosts, inline-code runtimes and disk-management verbs reach execution without naming a delete verb. The last block is ordinary work that must stay pass.",
